{"id": "EUVD-2026-103562", "enisaUuid": "bd042af0-0142-353b-ab4f-82fffc6c04aa", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/uv: Prevent potential out-of-bounds read\n\nWhen the system has more than 85 secrets, the uv_secret_list struct\narray only holds up to 85 items per page, resulting in an out of bounds\nread in find_secret_in_page if the targeted secret is in the next page\nor not stored at all.\n\nFix this by looping over the number of stored secrets which is the\nper sub-list count of stored secrets and not the overall count.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04bb5b2eb9f1d56110f14d3a4e31fa2c65fb026f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/116bba758533a139bbede8d717a1371bd6d890f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f47190b08b71e8482072978373ee88cb2dfbdaf4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-88ff-f8f3-f4qh", "CVE-2026-98648"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05d645c4-f664-3ce9-9986-53a77229e43e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c9137af2042e0d67aae0ccd84afc8ffc4b0d95d <116bba758533a139bbede8d717a1371bd6d890f6"}, {"id": "202affe9-d9d6-3c3e-aadc-7f4a27bac54d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c9137af2042e0d67aae0ccd84afc8ffc4b0d95d <f47190b08b71e8482072978373ee88cb2dfbdaf4"}, {"id": "3b845b5e-d525-38b1-b097-11b061755d83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "6ac52aa8-39e8-30f6-bd04-f96cb4387a06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9ed0de66-b7fe-3356-aef7-2a0190d7fdc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b6291eb3-1b6a-3b56-ad64-16fca88b9873", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "p